  "description": "Writes Invarix.Gate tool-call verdicts into an Invarix.Guard.Evidence decision log. Each verdict the action firewall renders is mapped to a CloudEvents 1.0 decision record: the tool that was asked for, the SHA-256 digest of the exact canonical arguments, each rule that matched as a detector result, the outcome, and, when the approval broker reported one, the operator who approved or refused an escalation. An escalation resolved with no decision from the broker, after an approval timeout or a broker failure, is recorded with no operator and says whether the call ran under the approval-timeout policy. Mapping runs on the tool-call thread and the write is handed to a bounded background queue, so a tool call never waits on an evidence write and a failed write never fails the call. A full queue evicts its oldest record, and each eviction and failed write is counted. Needs a Gate license token in observe and enforce mode alike, checked at registration and by the bridge's constructor, free for a company under the Community revenue threshold and paid above it. Terms: https://invarix.dk/gate.",
